Maya (design): Quick design check — proposing we drop ghost/secondary button height to 32px on compact surfaces so it lines up with the new condensed table row. Also a related nit: when a modal is open the floating toolbar toasts currently overlap the toolbar controls — propose to make toasts sit above toolbar but below modal overlay. Thoughts? :thinking_face:

Sam (frontend): Leaning +1 on the visual, but worried about hit target <44px. @Aria any accessibility concerns? Also can we avoid increasing z-index chaos if we add another layer?

Aria (a11y): Hit target must remain >=44px. Visual 32px is ok if we preserve an invisible touch area (padding) to meet 44px. For toasts: use `role="status"` + `aria-live="polite"` so assistive tech hears them. If they float above the toolbar make sure they don’t steal focus.

Leo (devex): Implementation idea: keep `height: 32px` but set `min-width` & extra `padding` for touch. Example snippet:```css
.ghost-btn {
  height: 32px;
  min-height: 32px;
  padding-inline: 12px; /* keeps visual width */
  touch-action: manipulation;
  /* invisible hit target */
  --hit-target-vertical: max(44px, 32px);
}
```

Sam (frontend): For spacing tokens — I'm worried about churn. Current tokens: `--space-compact-1/2/3`. Folks have proposed renaming to `--space-x-compact` which would be a breaking change. My suggestion: alias new names to old ones for one release. Example mapping in token file:```json
{
  "--space-compact-1": "8px",
  "--space-compact-2": "12px",
  "--space-compact-3": "16px",
  "aliases": {"--space-compact-1": "--space-1-compact"}
}
```

Maya (design): Agree with alias approach — avoid forcing every consumer to update. For toasts z-index plan: `--z-toolbar: 800`, `--z-toast: 900`, `--z-modal-overlay: 1000`. Toasts should be `pointer-events: none` by default so they don’t block toolbar clicks. If we need interactive toasts we can make an explicit interactive variant. :white_check_mark:

Leo (devex): I can put together a PR: alias tokens + update ghost btn CSS + add toast `pointer-events: none` and `role/status` attributes. Will also add a tiny visual regression test for compact tables + buttons stacking.

Sam (frontend): Draft PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/ui/pull/1234 (WIP) — includes token aliases and `--z-toast` addition. Please review before I flip the alias flag. @Maya @Aria

Aria (a11y): Quick checklist for PR:
- keep invisible hit targets >=44px
- toasts use `role="status"` and `aria-live="polite"`
- interactive toasts must be focusable and not `pointer-events:none`
- keyboard flow unaffected when toasts show up over toolbar
I'll test VoiceOver/JAWS on the branch once it's up.

Maya (design): SGTM. Let's canary this in staging. If the visual/regression tests look good merge after one design + one a11y review. Thanks everyone :rocket:

